Shortest Path
-------------
Source: https://github.com/Skretzo/shortest-path
Commits: 37abff3a3345185fc11fccecae04d8170de25a11 (1.21.3): the travel atlas, built 2026-10-25, and
         walk-grid.bin, rebuilt 2026-11-01 with every stop but the underwater one;
         7e81a40d0312e767fd7833637e57caae80a80253: where the plugin's own ways land (AtlasLinks) and the
         one bank the atlas can't reach (AtlasBanks)
Used in: src/main/resources/com/farmrunautopilot/atlas/ and data/travel/atlas/ (which reads it),
         walk-grid.bin and data/travel/WalkGrid.java, data/poh/HousePortal.java, run/FairyRingLog.java,
         and the travel data that names this notice

Facts: teleport landing tiles, bank locations, transports and hops with their ticks, menu text and object and NPC
ids, the levels, quests, items and game values each needs, where Teleport to House lands for each house location,
and walking distances, worked out with its own pathfinder and collision map by tools outside the plugin (tools/walk,
tools/atlas). One routine follows its code: FairyRingLog finds the leg's code in the fairy ring travel log and
scrolls to it as ShortestPathPlugin.scrollFairyRingPanel does. Nothing from Shortest Path is downloaded or loaded at
runtime. Its licence names no copyright holder, so it is credited to Skretzo and the Shortest Path contributors.

tools/atlas (dev only, not part of the plugin) compiles Shortest Path's own code, unchanged, from a local clone to
run its pathfinder with pretend accounts. That code is not in this repository, and the plugin ships none of it.
Its answers are shipped as data in src/main/resources/com/farmrunautopilot/atlas/ (places, ways, teleports, hops,
transports and requirements: tiles, ticks, menu text, object and NPC ids, and the requirement values from Shortest
Path's transport files).

